@* D7/D19 §3, §8 block B: the first InteractiveServer island in the app -- everything else stays Static
   SSR (D7). Mounted only inside WikiPage.razor's rendered-body branch, so it never exists for an
   ambiguous, refused, or not-found route -- exactly the routes IPageChangeNotifier could never
   meaningfully address anyway (PushReactionService's own remarks). *@
@* Self-declared here, not `@rendermode="InteractiveServer"` at WikiPage.razor's usage site --
   this component's whole purpose is a live circuit, so its render mode is intrinsic to what it is
   rather than a caller's choice, and self-declaring is what StaticSsrRenderModeTests' own reflection
   tripwire (RenderModeAttribute on the component's class) actually detects. *@
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@implements IDisposable
@using ZeroWiki.Content
@inject IPageChangeNotifier Notifier

@if (_changedOnDisk)
{
    <p class="page-changed-on-disk" role="status">
        This page has changed on disk since it was loaded.
        <a href="@_pageHref">Reload</a> to see the latest version.
    </p>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's own canonical route (D12), in its raw <see cref="EncodedRoute.Value"/>
    /// form rather than as <see cref="EncodedRoute"/> itself (§12, <c>12.3</c> second pass) --
    /// <see cref="EncodedRoute"/> deliberately has no JSON surface, since a JSON converter for it
    /// would let external code construct one, defeating D17's internal-constructor invariant. A plain
    /// <see langword="string"/> crosses the Static SSR-&gt;circuit boundary natively, and
    /// <see cref="OnInitialized"/> rebuilds the <see cref="EncodedRoute"/> from it, in-assembly, where
    /// the internal constructor has always been reachable.</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <b>§12 remediation (supervisor finding).</b> The default of <see cref="string.Empty"/> exists only
    /// so this type compiles under nullable reference types -- <see cref="EditorRequired"/> is an
    /// analyzer diagnostic, not a runtime guarantee, so a future call site that omits this parameter
    /// would otherwise subscribe under <c>new EncodedRoute("")</c> in silence: a route no diff can ever
    /// name, the exact silent-no-broadcast class this section exists to close, wearing a different
    /// value. <see cref="OnInitialized"/> now refuses that call shape loudly instead.
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Route { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    private IDisposable? _subscription;
    private bool _changedOnDisk;
    private string _pageHref = string.Empty;
    private EncodedRoute _route;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        // §12 remediation: EditorRequired never runs at runtime, so this is the actual guard against a
        // call site that omits Route -- fail loudly here rather than silently subscribing under
        // EncodedRoute("").
        ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(Route);

        // Re-materialises the value WikiPage.razor's call site already produced via
        // PageRouteCodec.Encode on the SSR side -- this does not mint a new encoded route, it
        // reconstructs the one that crossed the boundary as a string.
        _route = new EncodedRoute(Route);
        _pageHref = $"/wiki/{_route.Value}";

        // Guards against subscribing during the static-SSR prerender pass, which this component also
        // runs through once before its real InteractiveServer circuit starts (D7's render-mode split):
        // a prerendered instance is discarded immediately, and a subscription registered on it would
        // never be disposed (its circuit never ends -- it never had one).
        if (RendererInfo.IsInteractive)
        {
            _subscription = Notifier.Subscribe(_route, OnPageChangedAsync);
        }
    }

    private Task OnPageChangedAsync()
    {
        _changedOnDisk = true;
        return InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    public void Dispose() => _subscription?.Dispose();
}
